From de093cd2d20d106549a9202d1ecb88a2dde8be77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Voice Bot <voicebot@local>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:51:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] lakeside r2 light encoding: exactly one linear ->
 Cocos-byte conversion on every light path (board, journey end, day AND night)

Cocos 3.8.8 reads DirectionalLight.color, Ambient sky/ground colours and the legacy-standard albedo uniform (mainColor) as
Color bytes/255 = linear. r2's call sites ran linearToSrgb8(param), and the v3.4 commit compensated with pre-encoded day params
only, so the NIGHT params (and the journey night targets) still went sRGB-as-linear (moon 0.635/0.710/0.898 instead of
0.36/0.46/0.78, sky ambient 0.114/0.188/0.333 instead of 0.012/0.03/0.09).
- lakesideCocosLightColor(lin) is now THE conversion: round(clamp(lin) x 255). Params (day and night) are authored linear.
- LakesideBoardBackground.applyDir (main light + ambient sky/ground) and LakesideJourneyAtmosphere.lakesideAtmosphereTarget
  (journey end values, also the day/night toggle) call it instead of linearToSrgb8; so the journey end == board bytes.
- Water fallback mainColor (line 181): legacy standard uses the albedo uniform directly (baseColor = albedo, no SRGBToLinear),
  so it is linear too: 243/255/255 -> 230/255/255 (= tint 0.9/1/1). Clear colour (line 200) and fog stay sRGB, untouched.
- Day look unchanged (same bytes as v3.4). Night: colours kept as authored; illuminance ratios re-derived so night/day keeps
  r2's balance per term (luminance): sun 1.0 -> 0.617 (moon/sun 0.857), ambient 0.6 -> 0.694 (hemisphere night/day 0.219).
- No control-flow change (day/night, journey, restore). Tests: new lakeside-light-encoding (byte contract, params linear,
  journey end == board in both modes, no linearToSrgb8/stacked conversion on light call sites, night balance);
  dirlight / water_fog / daynight / journey_atmosphere follow the convention.
